## How it works

{% steps %}

1. **Create.** Paste the secret, choose when it expires, and optionally add a passphrase the recipient must enter.

2. **Share.** Send the link through any channel you already use: chat, a ticket, email. You keep a separate [receipt](/en/share/your-receipt/) that shows whether it has been opened.

3. **Gone.** The recipient opens it once and the content is destroyed. Anyone who tries the link afterwards, including you, sees nothing.

{% /steps %}

## What protects your secret

- **Destroyed on view or at expiry.** Every secret has a lifetime, and nothing is kept after it is read. [Data protection](/en/security/data-protection/)
- **Encrypted in transit and at rest**, on every plan. Add a passphrase for anything you would not paste into email. [Best practices](/en/security/best-practices/)
- **You choose the region.** Data is processed and stored in the EU, UK, US, Canada or New Zealand. [Where your data lives](/en/security/where-your-data-lives/)
- **No trackers, no analytics, no marketing email.** We store only what the service needs to run. [Our principles](/en/security/our-principles/)
- **Open source.** Read the code, or run it on your own infrastructure. [GitHub](https://github.com/onetimesecret/onetimesecret)

Found a security issue? [Report it here](/en/security/vulnerability-disclosure/).

Not sure where to begin? [Start here](/en/start/) has the full map of these docs.
